# Decimal division with integer operands

Divides 7 by 2 in both operand orders to verify the integer is promoted
and the result stays an exact decimal, producing 3.50 either way.

>>> source
integer_value: int = 7
integer_divisor: int = 2
dividend: decimal = 7
decimal_divisor: decimal = 2

// Verifies the Decimal/Int promotion with the decimal operand first.
decimal_divided_by_integer: decimal = dividend / integer_divisor
print(decimal_divided_by_integer)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
integer_divided_by_decimal: decimal = integer_value / decimal_divisor
print(integer_divided_by_decimal)

<<< stdout
3.50
3.50

<<< stderr
